{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## 2026-11-03: implemented; Gerrit 3279 pushed\n\nRoot cause: commit `3bde5613718` changed `_opcert_trust_root` (`src/rebar/_opcert_verify.py`) to fall back own key -> pinned key -> the public key embedded in the SSHSIG envelope (`envelope_key`), returning no key (`foreign_key`) only under `verify.require_environment`. The messages in `env_identity.py` and 3 passages of `docs/concurrency.md` were not updated with it.\n\nScope found by a string grep, beyond the 2 messages: the module and `reidentification_warning` docstrings, `docs/concurrency.md` lines 1044/1056/1077, and the `.opcert-key` carry-over entry plus its docs table row (\"without it no existing attestation verifies, even with the matching .env-id\"). Once the warning was reworded, that entry contradicted the sentence above it in the same rendered message. It now states the measured hazard: under the old id, the first op-cert signed mints a new key (`_opcert_signing.py:362`), after which certs from the old key fail as `mismatch` unless that key is pinned (`test_cert_under_an_unpinned_previous_key_still_fails`).\n\nTests: `test_reidentification_warning_says_old_attestations_still_certify` and `test_divergence_report_says_old_attestations_still_certify` failed on origin/main (missing `verify.require_environment`; then the carry-over contradiction) and pass now. `test_env_identity_guard.py` + c21f + d909 suites: 53 passed. Old-phrase grep: 9 hits before, 0 after. `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0.\n\nCommit `957db322151`-lineage on Gerrit change 3279 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/3279)."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793758513734388001,"uuid":"58a250dd-9a79-4c91-8851-c4ac9d561797"}